documents.content:
Load DevKillerDB before enabling mutations. A loading flag must start true; a failed read leaves editing disabled and offers an explicit retry. Never interpret a failed read as an empty database. Use one record for related fields so a save is atomic at the record level. Persist inside event handlers, not an effect that also runs on initial mount.
Example loading:
useEffect(() => { let alive = true; window.DevKillerDB.get('state').then(value => { if (alive) { setState(value ?? {items: []}); setLoading(false); } }).catch(() => { if (alive) setError('Could not load saved data. Retry loading.'); }); return () => { alive = false; }; }, []);
For writes, guard duplicate clicks with a ref, which changes synchronously (a React state update alone can leave a same-tick race). Disable controls while saving. Compute a proposed state, await DB.set, then commit UI state; retain the previous state and show an error on failure:
if (savingRef.current) return;
savingRef.current = true; setSaving(true);
try { await window.DevKillerDB.set('state', next); setState(next); setError(''); }
catch { setError('Not saved. Your previous data was kept.'); }
finally { savingRef.current = false; setSaving(false); }
The action must use current state, not a stale closure. On reload verify that additions, edits and deletions survived. Do not write demo data into a previously saved record.

Load /__devkiller/db.js before app.js and load app.js with defer. Start with all mutation buttons disabled. Await DevKillerDB.get('state') before rendering editable data. A failed read is not an empty state; show Retry and keep mutations disabled.
Use a synchronous boolean lock around asynchronous writes:
let saving = false;
async function commit(next) {
  if (saving) return false;
  saving = true; renderBusy(true);
  try { await DevKillerDB.set('state', next); state = next; render(); return true; }
  catch { showError('Not saved. Try again.'); return false; }
  finally { saving = false; renderBusy(false); }
}
Validate and compute next before commit. Do not clear form inputs until commit returns true. An event handler must call event.preventDefault() on forms. Use textContent for user text. Verify persistence by adding and deleting a record, then reloading the page.

Give each new record a stable id from crypto.randomUUID(). Update and delete by id, never by visible row index: sorting and filtering change positions. React keys should use that id. Create immutable candidates:
const nextItems = items.map(item => item.id === editingId ? {...item, name: cleanName, quantity: nextQuantity} : item);
const afterDelete = items.filter(item => item.id !== deletedId);
Validate edits with the same rules as creation. Preserve fields that the form does not edit. Persist the entire proposed collection and only then commit visible changes. Cancel editing should not mutate the saved record. Do not use Date.now alone as an identifier for rapid additions. Verify editing one item while a filter is active does not change a different item.

Parse monetary text explicitly and store integer cents for ordinary fixed two-decimal currencies. Empty input, NaN, Infinity, zero or negative values must be rejected when a positive amount is required. Define whether comma decimal input is accepted; normalize it deliberately instead of depending on locale coercion.
For input restricted to two decimals:
const valid = /^\d+(?:[.,]\d{1,2})?$/.test(raw.trim());
const cents = valid ? Math.round(Number(raw.trim().replace(',', '.')) * 100) : NaN;
if (!Number.isSafeInteger(cents) || cents <= 0) reject();
Compute totals by summing cents. Format only at presentation, for example (totalCents / 100).toFixed(2). Do not repeatedly round each partial floating-point sum. Numeric input with value '' is not zero. Recompute totals after editing and deleting. If quantity multiplies price, validate the quantity separately and keep the resulting cents a safe integer. Test 0.10 + 0.20 = 0.30 and edits/deletes after reload.

Keep one canonical saved collection and derive visibleRows from search/category/status filters. Do not persist the filtered array over the canonical collection. Compute an overall total from all records when the request says ALL, even if only one category is visible. Compute a subtotal from visibleRows only when explicitly requested, and label it.
const visible = items.filter(item => selected === 'All' || item.category === selected);
const overallTotal = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.amountCents, 0);
Sort a copy, [...visible].sort(compare), rather than mutating the saved array during rendering. Map a visible row action back to its stable id. Empty results and empty database are different states; offer clearing filters only for the former. Test two categories, select one, verify the overall total remains unchanged, then reload and delete the selected row.

Call hooks at the top level of a component, before conditional returns, never inside a branch, loop or event callback. Effects that subscribe or start timers must return cleanup. A timer can use a functional state update to avoid a stale captured count:
useEffect(() => {
  if (!running) return;
  const timer = setInterval(() => setElapsed(value => value + 1), 1000);
  return () => clearInterval(timer);
}, [running]);
Do not list elapsed as a dependency merely to increment it; that would recreate the timer each tick. Stopping or unmounting must clear the interval. Avoid saving every timer tick; persist meaningful state on explicit actions. Derived totals can normally be computed during render instead of an effect that writes more state. Test start, stop, restart and switching screens.

# D01 — Incomplete requests: editable event details / dados ausentes, a definir

Use for event sites, business pages, catalogs and profiles when the request names the product but omits editorial details. This is a DevKiller product policy, not a web standard. Preserve every supplied fact. Missing content is not a failed application.

Represent unavailable details as null. Render “To be defined” (English) or “A definir” (Portuguese). Keep code and interactions complete. Do not invent dates, venue addresses, prices, contact links or testimonial evidence. Fictional content is appropriate only if the request authorizes a demo, clearly labeled. Missing art can use an original local SVG, not a broken image or a pretend photograph.

Example initialization for a request that supplied only an event name:
```js
const initial = {name: suppliedName, description: null, venue: null, date: null};
const show = value => value?.trim() || 'To be defined';
// Load saved content first; initial is only for a successful null read.
const saved = await window.DevKillerDB.get('event-details');
const details = saved ?? initial;
```
Build an Edit details form for the missing fields. Keep submitted values as plain text, normalize empty optional values to null, and await DevKillerDB.set before confirming. Preserve the current UI values on write failure and offer retry. A read failure must not initialize or overwrite the database. Reuse the app's existing editing flow. The local editor is not a protected administrator account.

Do not coerce a missing price to zero or label it free. Do not construct a countdown without a valid date, a map without an address, or a mailto link without an email. Explain any dependent action with “Add the event date to enable reminders”, and link to Edit details. Other sections remain usable. An essential unknown business rule is a pending decision, never an invented rule.

Acceptance: supplied name is unchanged; unspecified venue displays a placeholder; editing and reloading retains the venue; failed storage does not report success; no invalid-date output. Model-proposed QA must not demand facts never supplied. Record pending content in summary/limitations without blocking preview. This guidance cannot turn broken code into a passing test.

Sources: user instruction dated 2026-09-14; DevKiller content-v1; modules/stacks.mjs database contract. Authored guidance, not a claim that every generated app has been tested.

# D02 — Premium themed filters, dropdowns and navigation / menus seletores cores

Use for festival genre filters, category pickers, catalogs, navigation and dark/light branded sites. Treat the expanded options as part of the design, not only the closed trigger. Match surface, text, border, accent, radius, spacing and shadow tokens. Give selected options a checkmark or radio plus text; hover, focus and selected are distinct.

Choice of pattern: a few choices suit styled radio chips; a longer set suits a disclosure panel with native radios and a Done button. A native select remains useful in ordinary forms, but its OS popup is not fully controlled by appearance:none. Set the correct color-scheme and select/option foreground/background. A brand-critical filter should prefer the styled disclosure pattern, within allowed dependencies. Do not import shadcn, Radix or other unavailable packages just because a tutorial uses them.

An authored React skeleton (adapt labels, spacing, data and placement):
```jsx
function Filter({label, options, value, onChange}) {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
  const id = useId(), root = useRef(null), trigger = useRef(null);
  const close = () => { setOpen(false); trigger.current?.focus(); };
  useEffect(() => {
    const outside = e => { if (!root.current?.contains(e.target)) setOpen(false); };
    document.addEventListener('pointerdown', outside);
    return () => document.removeEventListener('pointerdown', outside);
  }, []);
  return <div ref={root} className="filter"
    onBlur={e => {if (!e.currentTarget.contains(e.relatedTarget)) setOpen(false);}}
    onKeyDown={e => {if (e.key === 'Escape' && open) {e.preventDefault(); close();}}}>
    <button ref={trigger} type="button" aria-expanded={open} aria-controls={id}
      onClick={() => setOpen(!open)}>{label}: {options.find(o=>o.id===value)?.label} ▾</button>
    {open && <div id={id} className="filter-panel">
      <fieldset><legend>{label}</legend>{options.map(o =>
        <label key={o.id} className="filter-option"><input type="radio" name={id}
          value={o.id} checked={value===o.id} onChange={()=>onChange(o.id)}/>{o.label}</label>
      )}</fieldset><button type="button" onClick={close}>Done</button>
    </div>}
  </div>;
}
```
Import useState/useId/useRef/useEffect from React. Each instance owns its radio name. Keep real inputs keyboard accessible; style accent-color and label:has(input:checked). Tab enters/leaves; arrows select within the radio group; Space selects; Escape/Done closes and restores trigger focus. Keep the panel open during arrow navigation. Click-away must not steal focus from the outside target. Use an inline expanding panel for reliable containment, or explicitly measure available space for a floating panel. Set max-block-size and overflow:auto; never clip the panel under an ancestor's overflow:hidden. Use opaque surfaces. Size buttons for comfortable touch and visible focus. Native radios avoid a half-implemented ARIA listbox.

Navigation is a different component: nav with real links and disclosure buttons, aria-expanded, current-page indication, Escape and click-away. A mobile drawer needs a close action and should not rely on hover. Ordinary site navigation is not role=menu. Motion can be subtle and disabled under prefers-reduced-motion.

Sources consulted 2026-09-14:
- https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/disclosure/examples/disclosure-navigation/
- https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/radio/
- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/color-scheme

Authored implementation guidance; browser testing is not screen-reader certification.

# D03 — Responsive cards: prevent text/button overlap / espaçamento rótulos longos

Use for artist cards, schedules, products, toolbars and any heading with an adjacent action. A label and its add button require separate layout tracks. Do not absolutely position the action on top of text. The card grows when content wraps.

Authored CSS pattern:
```css
.card-head { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto; gap:1rem; align-items:start; }
.card-meta { min-width:0; margin:0; overflow-wrap:anywhere; line-height:1.5; }
.card-action { inline-size:2.75rem; min-block-size:2.75rem; padding:.5rem; }
.card-action svg { width:1.25rem; height:1.25rem; pointer-events:none; }
.cards { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,16rem),1fr)); gap:1rem; }
.card { padding:clamp(1rem,2vw,1.5rem); }
button:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:4px; }
```
Use a native button with an accessible name such as “Add Ava Meridian to my schedule”, not only “+”. Put the full stage/genre label in card-meta and the button in card-action. Avoid fixed card heights and arbitrary negative margins. Do not solve collision by reducing all typography or hiding meaningful words. Long translations, 200% zoom and narrow columns are normal content cases. A one-pixel rounding difference by itself is not a functional defect.

Verification: render short and long labels at 320, 391, 768 and 1440 CSS pixels; compare visible bounds of label and action for overlap, check the page is not horizontally overflowing, and click the action. Test focus separately. Decorative overlays must not receive pointer events. A screenshot reveals composition, while a successful click demonstrates an action; neither alone proves the other.

Sources consulted 2026-09-14:
- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/CSS_layout/Grids
- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/minmax

Authored layout recipe; adapt to the product rather than copying a whole page.

# S07 — Responsive app shell: no white bars / controles móveis faixas brancas display contents

Use para prevenir o problema observado no ROOMLAB: três botões móveis sem estilo e o X da biblioteca apareciam no desktop. A causa verificada foi agrupar .mobile-bar, .mobile-panel-head e .drawer-wrap em display:contents. Essa propriedade remove a caixa do elemento, mas mantém seus filhos visíveis. Não significa ocultar.

Padrão autoral mínimo para a shell (adaptar breakpoint):
```css
.mobile-bar,.mobile-panel-head{display:none}
.drawer-wrap{display:contents}
[hidden]{display:none!important}
button{font:inherit;color:inherit}
@media(max-width:760px){
  .mobile-bar{display:flex;gap:.5rem;background:var(--surface);padding:.5rem}
  .mobile-bar button{background:var(--surface);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border);min-height:44px}
  .mobile-panel-head{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between}
  .mobile-panel-head button{background:transparent;color:var(--text);border:0;min-width:44px;min-height:44px}
  .drawer-wrap{display:none}
  .drawer-wrap.open{display:block;position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:50}
}
```
O wrapper e os controles têm funções diferentes. Em react-v3, preferir Radix Dialog para drawer com foco, Escape e retorno ao trigger; ainda é necessário CSS e o trigger continua exclusivo do breakpoint certo. Não usar controles brancos padrão sobre texto branco. Não esconder um menu inteiro para disfarçar um botão sem função.

No desktop: ações essenciais visíveis, botões móveis ausentes. No celular: trigger visível, painel fechado inicialmente, abre por toque/teclado e fecha com Escape/ação explícita. Redimensionar não pode deixar overlay invisível prendendo cliques. Testar com texto longo, zoom e viewport estreito; um pixel de diferença não é uma reprovação funcional.

Fonte: causa confirmada no código gerado do ROOMLAB em 14/09/2026 e contrato de acabamento do Engine. Exemplo não altera automaticamente projetos existentes; correção deve preservar versão e dados.

# Q02 — Accessible Radix dialog and mobile navigation with complete CSS

Scope: react-v3, installed radix-ui umbrella package. Reference checked 2026-09-16: https://www.radix-ui.com/primitives/docs/components/dialog . Original minimal example; not copied upstream source. Radix supplies dialog interaction primitives; the application supplies styling, content and persistence.

Complete component, file src/components/DetailDialog.jsx:
```jsx
import { Dialog } from 'radix-ui';
import './detail-dialog.css';
export default function DetailDialog({title,description,children}) {
  return <Dialog.Root><Dialog.Trigger asChild><button type="button">View details</button></Dialog.Trigger><Dialog.Portal><Dialog.Overlay className="detail-overlay"/><Dialog.Content className="detail-panel"><Dialog.Title>{title}</Dialog.Title><Dialog.Description>{description}</Dialog.Description>{children}<Dialog.Close asChild><button type="button">Close details</button></Dialog.Close></Dialog.Content></Dialog.Portal></Dialog.Root>;
}
```
Complete stylesheet, file src/components/detail-dialog.css:
```css
.detail-overlay{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgb(0 0 0 / .45);z-index:40}
.detail-panel{box-sizing:border-box;position:fixed;top:50%;left:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);width:min(36rem,calc(100vw - 2rem));max-height:85dvh;overflow:auto;padding:1.5rem;background:var(--surface,#fff);color:var(--ink,#161616);border:1px solid var(--border,#aaa);border-radius:1rem;z-index:41}
.detail-panel button{font:inherit;cursor:pointer}
.detail-panel button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent,#1746ed);outline-offset:3px}
```
For a mobile drawer, adapt the position and dimensions, retain title, description and close control. Close after route selection. Scope rail-only icon styles under the rail, never a global selector that hides drawer labels. Verify Tab, Escape, focus return, readable theme colors and 320px viewport. Do not substitute unavailable @radix-ui/react-dialog imports for the installed radix-ui package.

# Q03 — Recharts analytics: responsive charts with real data and empty states

Scope: react-v3. Reference checked 2026-09-16: https://recharts.github.io/en-US/api/ResponsiveContainer/ . Original example using installed Recharts; container dimensions must be measurable.

File src/components/RevenueChart.jsx:
```jsx
import {ResponsiveContainer,BarChart,Bar,XAxis,YAxis,Tooltip} from 'recharts';
const dollars=n=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:2}).format(n/100);
export default function RevenueChart({rows}) {
  if(!rows.length)return <section><h2>Booking value</h2><p>No bookings in this period.</p></section>;
  const total=rows.reduce((sum,row)=>sum+row.cents,0);
  return <section aria-label="Booking value by month"><h2>Booking value</h2><p>{dollars(total)} across {rows.length} months.</p><div style={{height:280,width:'100%',minWidth:0}}><ResponsiveContainer width="100%" height="100%"><BarChart data={rows}><XAxis dataKey="month"/><YAxis tickFormatter={dollars}/><Tooltip formatter={value=>[dollars(Number(value)),'Booking value']}/><Bar dataKey="cents" fill="var(--accent, #ed5b20)" radius={[4,4,0,0]}/></BarChart></ResponsiveContainer></div></section>;
}
```
Caller supplies sorted rows shaped {month:'2026-10',cents:8400}, derived from saved reservations, with an explicit cancellation/status inclusion policy. Never seed unrelated random chart values. Recompute when reservations or filters change. Keep prices as integer cents and convert only for display. A grid parent should use minmax(0,1fr) to prevent chart overflow. Empty data and zero-valued data are different states. Test totals against the reservation table and inspect mobile tooltips.

# React Pro forms validation with React Hook Form and Zod

Supported only in react-v4. Checked 2026-09-16. Libraries installed: react-hook-form 7.88.0, @hookform/resolvers 5.9.1, zod 3.25.76. This is Zod 3; do not assume Zod 4-only methods. Primary reference: https://github.com/react-hook-form/resolvers

Complete minimal form component; compose it into the requested app. Persistence uses the supplied Engine API, not localStorage. Load existing records before allowing edits. Keep date/stock business rules in separate tested domain helpers. Form validation alone cannot provide transactional multi-user stock control.

```jsx
import {useRef,useState} from 'react';
import {useForm} from 'react-hook-form';
import {zodResolver} from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import {z} from 'zod';
const schema=z.object({quantity:z.number().int().min(1,'Choose at least one item')});
export default function QuantityForm(){
 const lock=useRef(false),[notice,setNotice]=useState('');
 const {register,handleSubmit,formState:{errors,isSubmitting}}=useForm({resolver:zodResolver(schema),defaultValues:{quantity:1}});
 const save=async data=>{if(lock.current)return;lock.current=true;setNotice('');try{await window.DevKillerDB.set('quantity',data.quantity);setNotice('Saved')}catch{setNotice('Could not save. Your entries are preserved.')}finally{lock.current=false}};
 return <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(save)} noValidate>
  <label htmlFor="quantity">Quantity</label>
  <input id="quantity" type="number" {...register('quantity',{valueAsNumber:true})} aria-invalid={!!errors.quantity} aria-describedby="quantity-error"/>
  <p id="quantity-error" role="alert">{errors.quantity?.message}</p>
  <button disabled={isSubmitting}>Save</button><p role="status">{notice}</p>
 </form>;
}
```

Use Controller for controlled Radix Select; never spread register onto a non-native control without adapting value/onChange. Preserve draft and dialog on save failure. An empty numeric input produces NaN rather than a meaningful zero: show a friendly error. Optional business details can use editable placeholders; missing optional content should not block the preview. Verify invalid input, keyboard focus, successful save/reload, failed save, and repeated submission.

# React Pro Tailwind accessible local UI components and visual composition

Supported only in react-v4. Checked 2026-09-16. Tailwind 4.3.3 with Vite plugin already configured. clsx, tailwind-merge and class-variance-authority installed. Radix primitives are available via radix-ui. shadcn is a source-component approach, not an importable shadcn package. No pre-existing @/components aliases. Deliver complete local components and relative imports.

Sources: https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation/using-vite and https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/installation/vite

Begin src/styles.css with @import "tailwindcss"; then add your theme CSS. Use complete literal class names, not constructed fragments like bg-${color}-500. Set root/body tokens so portals inherit them. Generated CSS is bundled locally; no CDN or runtime install. Use CSS custom properties or inline style for truly dynamic values.

Example src/components/ui/Button.jsx:
```jsx
import {clsx} from 'clsx';
import {twMerge} from 'tailwind-merge';
export function Button({className,type='button',...props}){
 return <button type={type} className={twMerge(clsx('inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-orange-600 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-orange-700 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-orange-600 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50',className))} {...props}/>;
}
```
Example src/components/ui/Modal.jsx:
```jsx
import {Dialog} from 'radix-ui';
export function Modal({open,onOpenChange,title,description,children}){
 return <Dialog.Root open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}><Dialog.Portal>
 <Dialog.Overlay className="fixed inset-0 z-40 bg-black/50"/>
 <Dialog.Content className="fixed left-1/2 top-1/2 z-50 max-h-[90dvh] w-[calc(100%-2rem)] max-w-lg -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 overflow-auto rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 text-zinc-950 shadow-xl">
 <Dialog.Title className="text-xl font-bold">{title}</Dialog.Title>
 <Dialog.Description className="my-3 text-zinc-600">{description}</Dialog.Description>
 {children}<Dialog.Close className="mt-4 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 focus-visible:outline-2">Close</Dialog.Close>
 </Dialog.Content></Dialog.Portal></Dialog.Root>;
}
```
If opened programmatically, explicitly restore focus to the opening control after closing. When using Dialog.Trigger, use asChild around one real button. Never nest buttons.

These examples establish behavior, not a mandatory orange visual identity. Choose typography, spacing, page structure and palette for the requested domain. Full application screens need loading/error/empty states and coherent photography, not repeated decorative cards. Responsive layout and accessibility remain necessary regardless of component libraries.
